</tbody></table></div>
<p class="note">On smaller screens, scroll the table horizontally to inspect all columns.</p>
<h2>What the evidence does <em>not</em> prove</h2>
<p>The association with installment count does not establish why the differences occurred. The available data do not identify whether they reflect interest, processing fees, adjustments or source-system errors. I therefore kept the two financial measures distinct and left discrepancies visible for further investigation instead of silently correcting them.</p>
<h2>What was tested</h2>
<p>The broader Snowflake/dbt pipeline includes 28 models and a documented regression result of 249 passing dbt checks, covering structural and business-rule integrity. Those checks are not equivalent to 249 independent scientific experiments, nor do they establish the economic cause of the differences. Incremental loading and idempotent reruns were also documented in the project.</p>
<h2>Inspect the evidence</h2>
<p>Technical reviewers can trace the numbers to the underlying SQL model, diagnostic queries and written findings. Readers without a technical background can start with the findings report.</p>
